      "title": "Google uses AI and proofs to make quantum programs leaner",
      "summary": "Google researchers used teams of AI agents plus computer-checked mathematical proofs to design quantum programs that need fewer computing resources. This matters because cutting the resources a program needs brings useful quantum calculations closer to what future machines could actually run. It is still a design technique, and the large, reliable quantum computers needed to run such programs at scale do not yet exist.",
